  No.01: WPS_GeoStatic
  #-----------------------
    ** Geographical Static Data
    -- address: https://www2.mmm.ucar.edu/wrf/users/download/get_sources_wps_geog.html
    -- including ALL　Mandatory (high-res) & Optional & Specific
        +++++++++++++++++++++++++ 
        *** When you have your own static data (e.g., custom land use, soil type, ...) that you 
            want to use instead of or in addition to the sahred "WPS_GeoStatic" data, 
            set the "geog_data_path" in your "namelist.wps" as a list of paths (ordered by priority);
            & you must also update the corresponding "filename" field in "GEOGRID.TBL" to match your custom
            subdirectory name, unless your data directory uses exactly the same name as the standard dataset.
            --------------------- 
            -- geog_data_path = 'path/to/your/own/data/', '/fsb/home/yutingwang/share/WPS_GeoStatic/'
            --------------------- 
        +++++++++++++++++++++++++ 


#@ Reanalysis/Analysis:
#>===========================
  No.01: 
  #-----------------------



#@ WRF Simulations: $dataDir/Data_WRFout
#>===========================
  #NOTES:
  #++++++++++++++++++++++
  *** When analyzing these data, it's better to remove the boundary buffer zones of each domain. 
  *** The boundary gird points (buffer region) are 5 for the mesoscale domain (d01-d04) & 24 for the LES domain.
  #++++++++++++++++++++++
  
  No.01: case01_Shenzhen
  #-----------------------
  (1) meso_202007_myj
    ** One month mesoscle simulation for Shenzhen, with MYU PBL scheme.
    -- resolution: 27/9/3/1 km for d01/d02/d03/d04; hourly for d01-d03 & 10-min for d04
 
  (2) meso_202007_ysu
    ** Same as (1) "meso_202007_myj", but with YSU PBL scheme.

  
  (3) les_20200730
    ** Mesoscale & microscale coupled modeling
    -- including:
        ++ meso-myj:     mesoscale simulation with MYJ pbl scheme   [dx: 27/9/3/1 km]
        ++ meso-ysu:     mesoscale simulation with YSU pbl scheme   [dx: 27/9/3/1 km]
        ++ les_100m-myj: large-eddy simulation forced by "meso-myj" [dx: 111 m]
        ++ les_100m-ysu: large-eddy simulation forced by "meso-ysu" [dx: 111 m]
    
    -- resolution: MESO: 27/9/3/1 km for d01/d02/d03/d04; hourly for d01-d03, 10-min for d04; 
                   LES: ~111m & 1-min for LES

  (4) les_20200713
    ** Mesoscale & microscale coupled modeling
    -- including:
        ++ meso-myj:         mesoscale simulation with MYJ PBL scheme [dx: 27/9/3/1 km]
        ++ meso-ysu:         mesoscale simulation with YSU PBL scheme [dx: 27/9/3/1 km]
        ++ les_100m-myj:     large-eddy simulation forced by "meso-myj" & MODIS@500m    [dx: 111m]
        ++ les_100m_gld-ysu: large-eddy simulation forced by "meso-ysu" & GlobeLand@30m [dx: 111m]
        ++ les_30m_gld-ysu:  large-eddy simulation forced by "meso-ysu" & GlobeLand@30m [dx: 37 m]
                             **Note: About 4 hours of "les_30m_gld-ysu" simulation output have been lost from the storage hard disks.

    -- resolution: MESO: 27/9/3/1 km for d01/d02/d03/d04; hourly for d01-d03, 10-min for d04; 
                   LES: ~111m & 1-min for LES


  No.02: case02_Typhoon_WindFarm
  #-----------------------
    ** Meso- & micro-scale coupled modeling for wind farm during Typhoon Mujigae (200909).
    -- including:
        ++ meso_Muji:         4-day mesoscale simulation  [res.: 27/9/3/1 km for d01-d04; hourly for d01-d03 & 10-min for d04]
        ++ les_100m_20090910: 1-day LES [res.: 111m & 1-min]
        ++ les_100m_20090911: 1-day LES [res.: 111m & 1-min] @The cell-perturbation intensity is different from "les_100m_20090910"

  

